NODE_ENV=development

# --- BUILD-TIME (required when building the image) -----------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* are inlined into the client bundle during `next build`. On
# EasyPanel they must go in the **Build args** tab (the Dockerfile declares them
# as ARG in the builder stage); setting them only in Environment/runtime does NOT
# change an already-compiled bundle. They must also exist at runtime, for the
# server code — on EasyPanel, set them in both places.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Public base URL, used to build password-reset links. Must be the address the
# customer's browser actually reaches, or the reset link points nowhere.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- RUNTIME-ONLY (never as a build arg) ---------------------------------------
# Server secret. Build args are baked into the image layers, so this key may only
# exist in EasyPanel's Environment (runtime) tab.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Optional (app notifications) — runtime
SMTP_URL=smtp://user:pass@host:587
MAIL_FROM=crm@example.com

# Block 11b. Where a scheduled routine that has gone quiet is reported. Optional
# — unset means /api/worker/health-alert sends nothing and says so, rather than
# the container refusing to boot over an alert address.
# The hourly check that calls it also needs, on the database:
#   alter database postgres set app.health_alert_url = 'https://<host>/api/worker/health-alert';
ALERT_EMAIL=ops@example.com

# Meta Embedded Signup — where a Station pairs its own WhatsApp Business account
# with this product (Templates → WhatsApp, visible to the Organization owner).
# Optional: unset means that card says the pairing is not configured instead of
# the container refusing to boot.
#
# Deliberately NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_ even though the value is public: set it in
# EasyPanel's Environment (runtime) tab and restart. No rebuild, and it must NOT
# go in Build args.
#
# The app_id below is a PLACEHOLDER — replace it with the real Meta app id.
# Must be https; any other scheme is ignored and the card renders as unconfigured.
WHATSAPP_EMBEDDED_SIGNUP_URL=https://business.facebook.com/messaging/whatsapp/onboard/?app_id=000000000000000

# --- Google Maps Platform (Block 28) -------------------------------------------
# TWO KEYS, NOT ONE, because the two halves need opposite restrictions and a
# single key can carry only one set.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY ships inside the page — that is what NEXT_PUBLIC_
# means — so the only protection it can have is an HTTP REFERRER restriction.
# In the Google Cloud console: Application restrictions -> Websites, and API
# restrictions -> Maps JavaScript API only.
#
# WRITE THE PATTERNS WITH `/*` ON THE END. Not the hostname — the pattern:
#
#     https://pulchatx.com/*
#     https://*.pulchatx.com/*
#
# A bare `https://pulchatx.com` authorises that ONE URL and nothing under it, so
# the home page works and every screen fails — including the only two that carry
# a map. This cost a production afternoon on 2026-08-17, and the symptom names
# the trap if you read it closely: the console says
# `RefererNotAllowedMapError ... Your site URL to be authorized:
# https://pulchatx.com/dashboards/music`, naming a PATH, because the path is
# what did not match. The second line covers `www.` and any other subdomain.
#
# The key is inlined at `next build`, so it belongs in EasyPanel's Build args and
# changing its VALUE needs a rebuild. Changing its RESTRICTION does not — that
# lives at Google and takes a few minutes to propagate.
#
# GOOGLE_GEOCODING_KEY never leaves the server; only the worker's drain uses it.
# Application restrictions -> IP addresses, listing wherever the worker runs,
# and API restrictions -> Geocoding API only. Runtime Environment tab, no
# rebuild. Giving the browser key geocoding rights would let anyone reading the
# page spend the account's quota.
#
# BOTH OPTIONAL. Unset means the maps are off: the geography panel renders one
# muted line saying so and the ranked tables underneath are unchanged. That is
# design D6, not a degraded mode to be fixed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=
GOOGLE_GEOCODING_KEY=

# Selects the fixture geocoder for the test suites. OPT-IN ONLY — an unset value
# is the real client — so no deployment can serve fixtures by accident. Never set
# this in EasyPanel.
# GOOGLE_FAKE=1

# --- NEVER set at runtime ------------------------------------------------------
# SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION=1 exists only inside the Dockerfile builder stage, because
# during `next build` the secrets legitimately do not exist. If that variable
# leaks into EasyPanel's runtime environment, `src/lib/env.ts` falls into the
# loose branch (`parseLooseEnv`), boot validation silently disappears and the
# container starts with no Supabase configuration at all — failing on the first
# query, in production, instead of failing at boot.
